Synced DHCP domains under a broader inline suffix.

The render puts the corp lane's synced DHCP domains in one rule-set rule
(corp-sync-domains.json) placed after every inline suffix rule, so sing-box
consults them only when no inline suffix matched. That changes one ranking:
`hq.shadow.example` (synced, corp) under escape's `shadow.example` used to win
on length and now loses — a hand entry wins, as corp sync promises. `explain`
must rank the same way, and both implementations must agree on it:

    x.hq.shadow.example      ->  ESCAPE  (escape's shadow.example)
    x.synced.corp.example    ->  CORP    (the inline corp.example, not the synced entry)
    a.dot.synced.example     ->  CORP    (synced only — nothing inline covers it)

The CIDR block is there so the render's corp-cidr set carries a synced CIDR
next to the hand-added one.
